          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "مخالفة — mukhālafa — \"an offence; a traffic ticket\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "حصل أبي على مخالفة أمس. ḥaṣala abī ʿalā mukhālafa ams. My father got a traffic ticket yesterday."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "مخالفة (mukhālafa) is built on the native Arabic root kh-l-f (Lane), the root of the taught khalfa, behind. Mukhālafa is the verbal noun of Form III, \"going against\" a rule."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
